At the TempleOS shell, JIT-compile this exact callback:

U0 Cross(CTask *, CDC *dc) {
  dc->color=YELLOW;
  GrLine(dc,ms.pos.x-16,ms.pos.y,ms.pos.x+16,ms.pos.y);
  GrLine(dc,ms.pos.x,ms.pos.y-16,ms.pos.x,ms.pos.y+16);
}

Install it with Fs->draw_it=&Cross;. Move the pointer to at least two
distinct positions and observe the live yellow cross following it.
Right-click in the top menu bar, open the built-in help index, and click
its Command Line documentation link. Keep the same callback installed
throughout; do not clear, replace, or reinstall it.
Move the pointer to two distinct positions over the opened document.
Finish with Command Line Overview open and the cross still following
the pointer over the document.

